{%- comment -%}
  What the studio makes to order. Brief §9.2, and the same three names the home
  page's custom band lists as labels.

  One card per service: the photograph, the name, and one sentence of what it
  covers. The split between this section and the band on the home page is
  deliberate — the band names the services, this section explains them. Putting
  the explanations in both places makes the home page a worse version of this
  page and gives the studio two copies of the same sentence to keep in step.

  NO ICONS. The design direction asks for minimal icons and an editorial look,
  and three marks in circles above three headings is the layout every services
  section has. The photograph is the mark. Nothing here needs an icon set
  extended, which also means nothing here needs a glyph invented for a service.

  4:5 CROPS, not squares. These are garments on people; a portrait crop is what
  the design's own product cards use and it is the ratio a uniform photograph is
  actually shot at. The crop is set here rather than read from the file so all
  three cards are the same height whatever the studio uploads — one landscape
  shot among three portraits would otherwise stagger the row of headings under
  them.

  Every card renders its labelled placeholder at final size until the studio
  sends project photography, which is the state this section ships in.

  ASSET FALLBACK ADDED 2026-09-22: the studio's B2B photography (see
  `selected-projects.liquid`) already exists and stands for these same three
  services, so each block now carries a `Shipped asset filename` alongside
  the image picker, rendered through `media-asset` exactly as
  `selected-projects` does. Per-block mapping: `project-hospital.webp` for
  Uniforms, `project-corporate.webp` (the two-tone corporate shirt) for Custom Apparel,
  `project-merchandise.webp` (the tote) for Merchandise & Special Projects.
  An `image` uploaded in the theme editor still overrides the shipped asset.
{%- endcomment -%}

<section aria-labelledby="custom-services-heading" class="mx-auto w-full max-w-content px-gutter py-section">
  <div data-reveal class="flex flex-col gap-4">
    <h2 id="custom-services-heading" class="text-h1 leading-h1">
      {% render 'copy', value: section.settings.heading, label: 'heading' %}
    </h2>

    {%- if section.settings.body != blank -%}
      <p class="wl-measure text-body leading-body text-ink-muted">{{ section.settings.body }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  <ul class="mt-block grid gap-7 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
    {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
      <li data-reveal class="flex flex-col gap-4.5" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
        {%- comment -%}
          `fit: 'contain'` because the shipped assets are the same alpha
          cut-outs `selected-projects` uses — a garment trimmed to its own
          proportions, not a 4:5 photograph. `object-cover` would crop into
          the cut-out itself.

          `plate: false` ADDED 2026-09-22, on instruction ("jelek banget...
          ga sesuai theme") — the default `bg-tone` letterbox (taupe-300)
          behind a `contain`-fit cut-out read as a flat coloured rectangle
          around the garment rather than a photograph, and it clashed with
          the page. Dropping it lets the section's own ground show through
          instead, the same effect `selected-projects` gets from its
          `plate: false` — the difference is that section wraps its call in
          its own padded plate div and this one does not, so here the
          garment sits directly on the page with no surface step at all.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {% render 'media-asset',
          image: block.settings.image,
          asset: block.settings.asset,
          alt: block.settings.alt,
          fit: 'contain',
          plate: false,
          ratio: '4 / 5',
          sizes: '(min-width: 1024px) 30vw, (min-width: 640px) 46vw, 92vw',
          asset_width: 1200,
          asset_height: 1500,
          label: 'Service photo' %}

        <h3 class="text-h2 leading-h2 tracking-h2">
          {% render 'copy', value: block.settings.title, label: 'service name' %}
        </h3>

        <p class="text-body leading-body text-ink-muted">
          {% render 'copy', value: block.settings.body, label: 'service description', lines: 2 %}
        </p>
      </li>
    {%- endfor -%}
  </ul>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Custom services",
  "max_blocks": 6,
  "settings": [
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Only list a service the studio actually produces. A card here is a promise that an enquiry about it will be answered." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Services" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Intro" }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "service",
      "name": "Service",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Name" },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Description" },
        { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Photograph", "info": "Overrides the shipped asset below. Empty with no shipped asset either renders a labelled placeholder at final size." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "asset", "label": "Shipped asset filename" },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "alt", "label": "Alt text", "info": "Used by the shipped asset only." }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Custom services",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "service", "settings": { "title": "Uniforms", "body": "For companies, schools, and organizations." } },
        { "type": "service", "settings": { "title": "Custom Apparel", "body": "Tailored pieces developed around your brand and requirements." } },
        { "type": "service", "settings": { "title": "Merchandise & Special Projects", "body": "For events, communities, campaigns, and collaborations." } }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
